## 1. Metadata, per page

- **Title:** target roughly 50 to 60 characters as a truncation heuristic. Google truncates by pixel width, not character count, and rewrites weak titles, so there is no hard limit. Primary keyword early, brand appended through the title template. Flag boilerplate, half empty, or keyword stuffed titles, since those are the ones Google rewrites.
- **Description:** target roughly 150 to 160 characters. Unique, accurate, self contained. Google rewrites most descriptions, so accuracy beats cleverness. Still worth doing well, since descriptions feed citation text on AI surfaces.
- **Canonical:** absolute URL, self referencing, on every page. App Router: `alternates.canonical` plus `metadataBase` set once in the root layout. Never canonical to elsewhere combined with noindex.
- No duplicate titles or descriptions across pages.
- **Robots:** index and follow for public pages, noindex for thank you and admin routes. A true 404 does not need noindex, the status handles it. Flag any soft 404 served as a 200.
- **Viewport:** configured through the `viewport` export, not inside `metadata`.
- **OpenGraph:** og:title, og:description, og:url, og:siteName, og:type, og:image at 1200 by 630 with an absolute URL.
- **Twitter:** twitter:card as summary_large_image, plus title, description, image.

