## 2. Schema and JSON-LD, per page type

All schema is JSON-LD in `<script type="application/ld+json">`. Use `@id` for entity linking. No duplicate entity declarations. Validate against schema.org types only. Never add a property not reflected in visible page content.

**Frame schema correctly for 2026.** Google's May 15, 2026 AI guide confirms schema is not required for AI Overviews or AI Mode, and there is no AI specific schema to add. So treat structured data as two things: the path to rich results in traditional Search, and entity clarity that helps Google's Knowledge Graph understand who and what a page is. That entity clarity is connective tissue, not a direct lever on AI citation. Do not spend effort on markup whose only claimed payoff is an AI surface.

**Deprecation status, flag anything chasing a dead rich result:** FAQ rich results ended for all sites in May 2026. HowTo ended Sept 2023. Sitelinks search box (SearchAction) ended Nov 2024. Also gone: Course Info, Claim Review, Estimated Salary, Special Announcement, Vehicle Listing (June 2025), and Q&A, Dataset, Practice Problems (Jan 2026). FAQPage and Service remain valid schema.org types and may stay for entity clarity and non Google consumers, but flag any effort spent on them expecting a Google rich result.

| Page type | Required schema |
|---|---|
| Homepage | Organization (@id, logo, sameAs, contactPoint), WebSite (no SearchAction, deprecated) |
| LocalBusiness or multi location | LocalBusiness or MedicalOrganization per location, with address, geo, openingHours, areaServed |
| Service pages | Service (entity clarity only, no rich result), BreadcrumbList. FAQPage optional |
| Team or About | ProfilePage where one person is the subject, Person per member, Physician for medical staff (medicalSpecialty, boardCertifications, hospitalAffiliations), which feeds knowledge panels |
| Blog or Article | Article (headline, datePublished ISO 8601, dateModified, author Person, publisher linking to the Organization @id), BreadcrumbList |
| Contact | LocalBusiness, BreadcrumbList |
| Reviews shown on page | AggregateRating or Review markup matching the visible review data exactly |
| Products | Product |
| Events | Event |
| All non homepage | BreadcrumbList minimum |
| Page types not listed | WebPage plus BreadcrumbList as a baseline fallback |

