## 3. E-E-A-T signals

Aligned with the September 2025 Quality Rater Guidelines update. Trust remains paramount. YMYL now explicitly includes civic and election information. AI assisted content is judged by the same standard as any content.

- Every article: a visible author name linked to a bio page.
- Author bio pages carry credentials, qualifications, experience.
- Healthcare and clinical pages: a "Medically reviewed by [Name], [Credentials]" block with a link, plus "Last reviewed: [Date]".
- Clinical and service pages: a numbered references section linking to .gov, .edu, or peer reviewed sources with `rel="noopener noreferrer"`.
- Trust signals near CTAs: credentials, certifications, insurance accepted, ratings. Only claims that are true and verifiable. Never fabricate.
- No generic author attribution ("Admin", "Staff").

