## 6. Technical SEO

- XML sitemap at `/sitemap.xml` through the App Router `sitemap.ts` convention. All public pages, no noindex pages.
- `robots.txt` through `robots.ts`: disallow /admin, /api, staging and filtered or duplicate URLs, declare the sitemap, verify the AI crawler policy from section 4.
- Clean URLs, no query params on main pages.
- Breadcrumb navigation on all non homepage pages.
- HTTPS enforced.
- No console errors on any page.
- No redirect chains (301 to 301 to final).
- No canonical or redirect conflicts.
- Images: AVIF first with WebP fallback (`formats: ['image/avif', 'image/webp']`), descriptive file names, lazy loaded below the fold, `next/image` throughout, `sizes` defined.
- LCP image uses `loading="eager"` and `fetchPriority="high"`. Flag any use of the deprecated `priority` prop on Next 16.
- Fonts loaded through `next/font`, self hosted, `font-display: swap`, automatic size adjusted fallback metrics for zero font swap layout shift. Flag any external font CSS or manual `@font-face` without size adjusted fallbacks. Prefer a single variable font file per family over multiple static weights.
- Core Web Vitals at the 75th percentile: LCP at or under 2.5s, INP at or under 200ms, CLS at or under 0.1. INP replaced FID in 2024. Do not use the old 100ms FID number.
- Lighthouse is a diagnostic, not the score that ranks. The ranking signal is field data from CrUX. Use Lighthouse to find issues, then verify against PageSpeed Insights field data. Target 90 or above on mobile as a lab proxy.
- Mobile: responsive, no horizontal scroll at 360px, touch targets 44px.
- Click to call: every phone number is a `tel:` link on mobile.

**2026 platform items to check.** These are newer than most audit templates and are easy wins:
- `text-wrap: balance` on headings and `text-wrap: pretty` on body. Flag pages where headlines drop orphan words or body has single word last lines.
- Reusable components use container queries rather than viewport breakpoints for their internal layout, which reduces layout shift across contexts.
- Menus, tooltips, and dropdowns use anchor positioning and the Popover API or a customizable `<select>`, not a scripted custom widget, which improves the keyboard and focus story.
- `field-sizing: content` on textareas.

